-- Petrobrain in-cockpit text overlay (BL-2.5) -- widget/skin definition.
--
-- Deploy alongside petrobrain-overlay-hook.lua to
-- `Saved Games\DCS\Scripts\Hooks\petrobrain-overlay.dlg` (see
-- aircraft-layer/WORKFLOW.md). Loaded via
-- `DialogLoader.spawnDialogFromFile(lfs.writedir() ..
-- "Scripts\\Hooks\\petrobrain-overlay.dlg", nil)`.
--
-- UNVERIFIED AGAINST A LIVE DCS SESSION as of authorship -- see
-- plans/dcs-text-panel-output/plan.md Stage 2.
--
-- Structure modeled on two real, installed reference files, read in full
-- this session (see
-- aircraft-layer/research/2026-09-09-dcs-text-panel-output-channel.md):
--   - $DCS_SAVED_GAMES_PATH/Mods/services/DCS-SRS/UI/DCS-SRS-Overlay.dlg
--     (Window root, draggable, a Panel child for the background box).
--   - $DCS_INSTALL_PATH/Scripts/UI/gameMessages.dlg (DCS's own shipped
--     AutoScrollText usage -- `type = "AutoScrollText"`, a `skin.skins.text`
--     sub-skin overriding color/font/fontSize/shadow only). Its base skin,
--     $DCS_INSTALL_PATH/dxgui/skins/skinME/auto_scroll_text.skin.lua, already
--     sets `textWrapping = true` on that same "text" sub-skin by default
--     (Session 2 Finding 17) -- not re-declared below for the same reason
--     gameMessages.dlg's own real instances don't re-declare it either.
--
-- One child differs from both references: a single AutoScrollText widget
-- ("MessageText") is used directly, per the plan's Message Model, instead
-- of SRS's manually-stacked-Static array -- DCS's own native message system
-- already is "a small scrolling log of short text lines" (this project's
-- exact shape) and manages accumulate/expire natively via
-- addText()/clear(), so no per-line Y-offset bookkeeping is needed here.

